What is Enterprise WLAN?
Enterprise Wireless Local Area Network (WLAN) refers to scalable wireless infrastructure designed specifically for business environments, eliminating the need for physical cables through radio wave connectivity. These networks enable seamless communication across various enterprise settings - from corporate offices and manufacturing plants to educational campuses and healthcare facilities. The architecture typically includes wireless access points (APs), controllers, network interface cards, and switches, providing the backbone for modern digital workplaces.

